  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607197800: PostgreSQL Linux arm64 qualification

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

Linux arm64 is an observed platform, not merely a scheduled CI claim. The full
released interoperability program must pass as the non-root `postgres` user in
a clean Debian Bookworm container. Cancellation waits a fixed 100 ms after the
client write trace so that a cold or remote backend has dispatched the sleeping
statement; without this synchronization the test could consume a valid cancel
before the backend entered query execution.

## Evidence

PostgreSQL 15.18 on Linux arm64 with Temurin 21.0.11 passes TLS,
SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS, cancellation, all database protocol slices, concurrent FIFO
pooling, immediate crash recovery, TLS half-open recovery, credential and
certificate rotation, and the 90-operation contention soak. The disposable
container and Maven volume were removed and OrbStack returned to its prior
stopped state.

This closes one independently observed Linux platform cell. Linux x86_64
PostgreSQL 14/15/17 and weekly 3,000-operation freshness remain CI-owned gates."}]
